 rg/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Birdwatchers-2-Christine-Mansfield-16.9.jpg
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://houstonarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2
 023/07/Birdwatchers-2-Christine-Mansfield-16.9.jpg
UID:Iu8M7bSbxjOZSSkCa8G2x
SUMMARY:Second Saturday Bird Survey
DTSTAMP:20260719T101344Z
DTSTART:20260912T080000Z
DESCRIPTION:2nd Saturday of the month8:00 – 10:00 amFree\, but donations ap
	preciatedAll ages\, minors must be accompanied by an adult \n\n\n\nWork on
	 your bird watching skills while helping the Arboretum monitor bird popula
	tions on a fun\, relaxed morning walk. Join us on the second Saturday of e
	ach month in front of the Nature Center building for a two-hour bird surve
	y led by Arboretum staff members Kelsey Low and Theo Ostler. We welcome al
	l levels of bird watching skill and all ages (as long as you’re quiet) – b
	ut no dogs\, please!  \n\n\n\nIf you have binoculars of your own\, please 
	bring them. We have a limited number of binoculars available to borrow\n\n
	https://houstonarboretum.org/event/second-saturday-bird-survey/2026-09-12/
	\n\nFrom Houston Arboretum & Nature Center
URL:https://houstonarboretum.org/event/second-saturday-bird-survey/2026-09-
	12/
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:houston-arboretum
CATEGORIES:Houston Arboretum & Nature Center
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://houstonarboretum.o
 rg/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Guided-Nature-Hike-16x9-1.jpg
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://houstonarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2
 024/07/Guided-Nature-Hike-16x9-1.jpg
UID:FzgYLg0l6Isc37tbBZ9qh
SUMMARY:Guided Nature Hikes
DTSTAMP:20260719T101344Z
DTSTART:20260912T100000Z
DESCRIPTION:Select Saturdays (weather permitting)10:00 am – 10:45 am and 11
	:00 am – 11:45 amFreeAll ages\, minors must be accompanied by an adultHike
	s are limited to 20 spots on a first come\, first served basis. \n\n\n\nPl
	ease meet at the Information signage located between the 610 Parking Loop 
	and the Nature Center Building. \n\n\n\nVenture out with an Arboretum Guid
	e for a hike through the Houston Arboretum. Explore our ecosystems to lear
	n about the local wildlife\, plants\, and natural history of our beautiful
	 nature center. Hikes will vary but expect to spend 40-45 minutes on the t
	rail.  \n\n\n\nPlease come prepared for the outdoors. Closed toe shoes\, a
	 water bottle\, weather-appropriate hiking attire\, and bug spray are reco
	mmended. \n\n\n\nupcoming hikes\n\n\n\n\n\nEnglish \n\n\n\nSeptember 12Oct
	ober 3November 7December 5 \n\n\n\n\n\nEspañol \n\n\n\nSeptiembre 19Octubr
	e 10Noviembre 14Diciembre 12 \n\n\n\n\n\nNo groups\, please. Groups can bo
	ok a Private Group Tour during the week\, and Scout Groups can visit our G
	irl Scout and Boy Scout pages to book a private opportunity. \n\n\n\n\nGui
	ded Nature Hikes en español\n\nhttps://houstonarboretum.org/event/guided-n
	ature-hikes/2026-09-12/1/\n\nFrom Houston Arboretum & Nature Center
URL:https://houstonarboretum.org/event/guided-nature-hikes/2026-09-12/1/
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:houston-arboretum
CATEGORIES:Houston Arboretum & Nature Center
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT1H
